NFSv3 server tests
==================

This directory contains direct NFSv3 RPC tests for the 22 procedures in
RFC 1813, implemented using the NFSv3 XDR definitions in
`nfs4.1/xdrdef/nfs3.x` and the existing NFSv3 RPC client.

From this directory, generate the XDR modules and run the test suite with:

    (cd .. && python3 setup.py build)
    python3 testserver.py SERVER /export/path

The top-level build must run from the repository root, because it locates
the xdr, rpc, nfs4.1, and nfs4.0 directories relative to its working directory.
The subshell above returns you to nfs3 after the build.

The export must permit the selected AUTH_SYS credentials to create and remove
files and directories. The runner mounts the export through MOUNTv3, creates
a private test directory, runs the procedures, and removes its test objects.
Use `--list` to see all test cases, `--port PORT` to set the NFS port, and
procedure names (for example `READ WRITE COMMIT`) to run each selected
procedure together with its edge cases. A specific case can also be selected
by name (for example `READ_MAX_COUNT`). Edge cases include byte-exact,
non-UTF-8 filenames and symbolic-link targets, as NFSv3 XDR strings are opaque
byte strings and do not require UTF-8 encoding.
